<title>GERMANY: Suedzucker - 96/97 net profit above 95/96.</title>
<headline>Suedzucker - 96/97 net profit above 95/96.</headline>
<dateline>MANNHEIM, Germany 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>German sugar processor Suedzucker AG said on Wednesday that its net profit in its 1996/97 business year was clearly above levels seen a year ago.</p>
<p>The group also said that group sales in 1996/97 were 7.597 billion marks ($4.5 billion), up from 7.483 billion marks the previous year.</p>
<p>($ = 1.702 German Marks)  </p>
<p>Suedzucker said in its interim report that the profit hike came despite higher tax charges on revenues. The group did not give a concrete net profit figure.</p>
<p>The group said that progress in the year so far indicated that Suedzucker would continue to develop positively in the full business year.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
